main={55:('Factually Te Papa states blanket prints onto paper: one correct material among ink, plate, paper and blanket. However MAIN repeats materials6 paper as the material/support of book pages. Merely naming offset and final imprint does not ask a different property, stage operation or quantity; source gives richer process facts but the literal does not ask them. FIX for cross-topic semantic duplicate, not factual error.',[T,TR]),56:('Te Papa describes four colour inks and transfer of the inked image from plate to blanket to paper. Only printing ink supplies the colour; plate/blanket transfer it and paper receives it. One stable key, and alternatives are actual participants in the same process.',[T,TR]),58:('Berkeley distinguishes leaf attachment (thread/adhesive/staples), assembled book/text block, case and casing-in. Together these support binding as the general assembly-plus-cover process. Three wrong options are methods of attaching leaves/signatures, not the whole process explicitly requested including protective cover.',[B])}
